1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,760
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,719 --> 00:00:05,929
Earth.

3
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:07,889
Fire.

4
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:10,225
Air.

5
00:00:11,309 --> 00:00:14,771
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,313 --> 00:00:18,816
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,692 --> 00:00:22,570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,654 --> 00:00:23,738
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,821 --> 00:00:26,741
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,116 --> 00:00:28,368
100 years passed,

11
00:00:28,451 --> 00:00:30,995
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

12
00:00:31,079 --> 00:00:32,580
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:35,083
And although
his airbending skills are great

14
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:39,087
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:41,965
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:00:42,298 --> 00:00:43,967
[ ♪... ]

18
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:50,473
( MAN READING )

19
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:51,933
I need you, Zuko.

20
00:00:52,016 --> 00:00:56,771
I've plotted every move of this day,
and the only way we win is together.

21
00:00:59,607 --> 00:01:01,276
We've done it, Zuko.

22
00:01:01,359 --> 00:01:04,070
The Fire Nation has conquered Ba Sing Se.

23
00:01:04,153 --> 00:01:05,446
ZUKO: I betrayed uncle.

24
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:07,657
AZULA: No, he betrayed you.

25
00:01:08,575 --> 00:01:12,620
When you return home,
father will welcome you as a war hero.

26
00:01:12,704 --> 00:01:14,163
But I don't have the Avatar.

27
00:01:14,581 --> 00:01:16,541
What if father doesn't restore my honor?

28
00:01:19,502 --> 00:01:20,878
[ ♪... ]

29
00:01:28,052 --> 00:01:29,637
( GROANING )

30
00:01:35,518 --> 00:01:36,811
( GRUNTING )

31
00:01:41,316 --> 00:01:42,942
What happened?

32
00:01:49,032 --> 00:01:50,241
Oh, no!

33
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:59,208
( GRUNTING )

34
00:02:01,085 --> 00:02:02,795
MAN: You hear something?

35
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:04,422
( GASPING )

36
00:02:06,883 --> 00:02:07,884
MAN: He's awake.

37
00:02:08,551 --> 00:02:09,636
( PANTING )

38
00:02:09,719 --> 00:02:11,262
Stop, wait!

39
00:02:12,347 --> 00:02:14,223
( GRUNTING )

40
00:02:18,311 --> 00:02:19,312
Momo?

41
00:02:20,063 --> 00:02:21,356
( SQUEAKING )

42
00:02:24,025 --> 00:02:26,569
Twinkle-toes, that's got to be you.

43
00:02:27,862 --> 00:02:29,364
Aang, you're awake.

44
00:02:29,447 --> 00:02:30,573
AANG: Are you sure?

45
00:02:31,032 --> 00:02:32,867
I feel like I'm dreaming.

46
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:33,951
You're not dreaming.

47
00:02:34,243 --> 00:02:35,620
You're finally awake.

48
00:02:35,703 --> 00:02:38,289
Aang, good to see you
back with the living, buddy.

49
00:02:39,123 --> 00:02:40,166
Sokka?

50
00:02:40,917 --> 00:02:42,502
-( SIGHING )
- TOPH: Uh-oh, somebody catch him.

51
00:02:42,585 --> 00:02:43,795
He's gonna...

52
00:02:45,296 --> 00:02:47,590
( GROWLING )

53
00:02:56,349 --> 00:02:57,642
Aren't you cold?

54
00:02:58,893 --> 00:03:00,728
I've got a lot on my mind.

55
00:03:01,312 --> 00:03:03,231
It's been so long.

56
00:03:03,314 --> 00:03:05,441
Over three years since I was home.

57
00:03:06,609 --> 00:03:08,778
I wonder what's changed.

58
00:03:08,861 --> 00:03:10,571
I wonder how I've changed.

59
00:03:10,655 --> 00:03:12,824
( YAWNING ) I just asked if you were cold.

60
00:03:12,907 --> 00:03:15,201
I didn't ask for your whole life story.

61
00:03:17,662 --> 00:03:19,288
Stop worrying.

62
00:03:30,049 --> 00:03:32,176
AANG: Why are we on a Fire Nation ship?

63
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,262
Why is everyone dressed this way?

64
00:03:34,345 --> 00:03:37,306
And why am I the only one
who's completely out of it?

65
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:38,975
You need to take it easy, ok?

66
00:03:39,058 --> 00:03:41,018
You got hurt pretty bad.

67
00:03:42,937 --> 00:03:44,439
I like your hair.

68
00:03:44,522 --> 00:03:45,898
I have hair?

69
00:03:46,774 --> 00:03:48,151
How long was I out?

70
00:03:48,234 --> 00:03:49,569
A few weeks.

71
00:03:49,652 --> 00:03:50,862
Everything ok?

72
00:03:50,945 --> 00:03:52,113
We're fine, dad.

73
00:03:52,447 --> 00:03:55,408
I'm Hakoda, Katara and Sokka's father.

74
00:03:55,491 --> 00:03:58,077
He knows who you are.
I just called you "dad," didn't I?

75
00:03:58,828 --> 00:04:00,079
I guess you're right.

76
00:04:01,539 --> 00:04:04,000
Nice to officially meet you, Chief Hakoda.

77
00:04:04,083 --> 00:04:05,460
It's an honor to meet you.

78
00:04:05,793 --> 00:04:07,837
Great, great.
Now you guys have finally met,

79
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,881
so would you mind
giving us a little privacy?

80
00:04:10,757 --> 00:04:12,008
Of course.

81
00:04:14,343 --> 00:04:16,387
Are you mad at your dad or something?

82
00:04:17,096 --> 00:04:19,474
What? Not at all. Why would you say that?

83
00:04:19,974 --> 00:04:21,392
( SHRUGS, GROANS )

84
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:23,770
Maybe we should go upstairs.

85
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,897
You need a healing session.

86
00:04:31,277 --> 00:04:33,529
Tell me where your pain
feels most intense.

87
00:04:33,613 --> 00:04:35,406
( GRUNTING ) A little higher.

88
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:36,491
( GRUNTS )

89
00:04:43,998 --> 00:04:45,124
Wow.

90
00:04:45,208 --> 00:04:47,460
You're definitely in the right area there.

91
00:04:47,835 --> 00:04:50,630
I can feel a lot of energy
twisted up around there.

92
00:04:50,922 --> 00:04:52,548
Let me just see if I can...

93
00:05:02,308 --> 00:05:03,643
I went down.

94
00:05:03,726 --> 00:05:05,436
I didn't just get hurt, did I?

95
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:07,146
It was worse than that.

96
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:10,191
I was gone, but you brought me back.

97
00:05:10,733 --> 00:05:13,486
I just used the spirit water
from the North Pole.

98
00:05:13,569 --> 00:05:14,821
I don't know what I did, exactly.

99
00:05:15,863 --> 00:05:17,281
You saved me.

100
00:05:17,782 --> 00:05:19,200
You need to rest.

101
00:05:22,203 --> 00:05:26,958
WOMAN 1: Your Princess Azula,
clever and beautiful,

102
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:32,672
disguised herself as the enemy
and entered the Earth Kingdom's capital.

103
00:05:32,755 --> 00:05:37,510
WOMAN 2: In Ba Sing Se,
she found her brother Zuko,

104
00:05:37,593 --> 00:05:40,471
and together, they faced the Avatar.

105
00:05:40,555 --> 00:05:46,310
BOTH WOMEN: And the Avatar fell,
and the Earth Kingdom fell.

106
00:05:46,394 --> 00:05:50,898
WOMAN 1: Azula's agents
quickly overtook the entire city.

107
00:05:51,274 --> 00:05:54,610
They went to Ba Sing Se's great walls...

108
00:05:54,694 --> 00:05:57,530
BOTH WOMEN: ...and brought them down.

109
00:06:05,496 --> 00:06:09,500
WOMAN 2: The armies of the Fire Nation
surged through the wall

110
00:06:09,584 --> 00:06:15,381
and swarmed over Ba Sing Se,
securing our victory.

111
00:06:16,132 --> 00:06:17,758
( BABY CRYING )

112
00:06:27,018 --> 00:06:30,354
BOTH WOMEN: Now the heroes
have returned home.

113
00:06:30,438 --> 00:06:34,066
WOMAN 1: Your princess, Azula.

114
00:06:34,150 --> 00:06:37,320
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

115
00:06:37,737 --> 00:06:42,700
And after three long years,
your prince has returned.

116
00:06:43,159 --> 00:06:44,493
Zuko.

117
00:06:45,745 --> 00:06:51,250
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

118
00:06:53,502 --> 00:06:56,547
After what happened in Ba Sing Se,
we had to get you to safety.

119
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:59,133
We flew back to Chameleon Bay,

120
00:06:59,216 --> 00:07:01,677
where we found my father
and the other water tribe men.

121
00:07:03,387 --> 00:07:06,349
The Earth King decided he wanted
to travel the world in disguise,

122
00:07:06,432 --> 00:07:07,767
so he set off alone.

123
00:07:07,850 --> 00:07:09,435
Well, not completely alone.

124
00:07:09,518 --> 00:07:10,686
( GROWLING )

125
00:07:13,814 --> 00:07:16,275
Soon, the bay was overrun
with Fire Nation ships.

126
00:07:16,359 --> 00:07:19,946
Rather than fight them all, we captured
a single ship and made it our disguise.

127
00:07:20,321 --> 00:07:22,323
Since then, we've been traveling west.

128
00:07:22,406 --> 00:07:24,492
We crossed through the Serpent's Pass
a few days ago.

129
00:07:25,034 --> 00:07:27,578
We've seen a few Fire Nation ships,
but none have bothered us.

130
00:07:28,663 --> 00:07:29,664
So, what now?

131
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:32,792
We've been working on
a modified version of the invasion plan.

132
00:07:33,042 --> 00:07:35,419
It's Sokka's invasion plan.

133
00:07:36,128 --> 00:07:37,922
Yes, Sokka's plan.

134
00:07:38,673 --> 00:07:42,051
We won't be able to mount a massive
invasion without the Earth King's armies

135
00:07:42,134 --> 00:07:45,721
But the solar eclipse will still
leave the Fire Nation vulnerable.

136
00:07:46,138 --> 00:07:47,848
So we're planning a smaller invasion.

137
00:07:47,932 --> 00:07:51,018
Just a ragtag team of our friends
and allies from around the Earth Kingdom.

138
00:07:51,102 --> 00:07:53,187
We already ran into
Pipsqueak and The Duke.

139
00:07:53,813 --> 00:07:55,481
Good to see you again, Aang.

140
00:07:56,023 --> 00:07:59,568
And the best part is, the eclipse
isn't even our biggest advantage.

141
00:07:59,652 --> 00:08:01,904
We have a secret.

142
00:08:02,488 --> 00:08:04,240
- You.
- Me?

143
00:08:04,323 --> 00:08:06,617
Yep, the whole world thinks you're dead.

144
00:08:07,076 --> 00:08:08,703
Isn't that great?

145
00:08:13,374 --> 00:08:14,375
[ ♪... ]

146
00:08:14,917 --> 00:08:16,252
The world thinks I'm dead?

147
00:08:16,794 --> 00:08:18,212
How is that good news?

148
00:08:18,295 --> 00:08:19,296
That's terrible.

149
00:08:19,672 --> 00:08:20,715
No, it's great.

150
00:08:20,798 --> 00:08:23,009
It means the Fire Nation
won't be hunting us anymore.

151
00:08:23,217 --> 00:08:26,095
And even better, they won't be
expecting you on the day of black sun.

152
00:08:26,178 --> 00:08:27,722
No, no, no, no, no.

153
00:08:28,139 --> 00:08:29,682
You have no idea.

154
00:08:29,765 --> 00:08:31,225
This is so messed up.

155
00:08:31,475 --> 00:08:33,978
( HORN BLARING )

156
00:08:34,311 --> 00:08:35,938
I'll handle this.

157
00:08:36,022 --> 00:08:37,356
The Avatar is back.

158
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,691
( GRUNTING )

159
00:08:39,191 --> 00:08:40,359
KATARA: Aang, wait.

160
00:08:40,443 --> 00:08:42,903
Remember, they don't know
we're not Fire Nation.

161
00:08:46,407 --> 00:08:48,534
Everyone, just stay calm.

162
00:08:48,617 --> 00:08:50,453
Bato and I will take care of this.

163
00:08:56,125 --> 00:08:58,669
I hate not being able to do anything.

164
00:08:58,753 --> 00:09:00,504
Hopefully, you won't need to.

165
00:09:13,059 --> 00:09:15,144
Commander, why are you off course?

166
00:09:15,519 --> 00:09:17,855
All western fleet ships
are supposed to be moving

167
00:09:17,938 --> 00:09:20,316
toward Ba Sing Se
to support the occupation.

168
00:09:20,733 --> 00:09:23,402
Actually, we're from the eastern fleet.

169
00:09:23,486 --> 00:09:25,154
We have orders to deliver some cargo.

170
00:09:25,488 --> 00:09:27,907
Ah, eastern fleet.

171
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:31,911
Well, nice of Admiral Chan to let us know
he was sending one of his ships our way.

172
00:09:32,328 --> 00:09:34,955
I'm sure Admiral Chan
meant no disrespect, sir.

173
00:09:35,039 --> 00:09:38,334
I mean, how hard is it to write a quick
note and send a hawk our way?

174
00:09:39,001 --> 00:09:42,379
Next time, we'll send two hawks,
to be sure you get the message.

175
00:09:44,632 --> 00:09:48,094
Sir, Admiral Chan has been on leave
for two months at Ember Island.

176
00:09:48,177 --> 00:09:51,472
What? Why doesn't anyone
ever tell me anything?

177
00:09:51,555 --> 00:09:52,765
Something's not right.

178
00:09:52,848 --> 00:09:54,016
They should've known that.

179
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,476
I think this is a captured ship.

180
00:09:56,685 --> 00:09:58,938
Just stay quiet
until we're safely across the ramp.

181
00:09:59,396 --> 00:10:01,398
Then we'll sink this ship.

182
00:10:02,483 --> 00:10:03,526
They know!

183
00:10:06,112 --> 00:10:07,404
( GRUNTING )

184
00:10:08,572 --> 00:10:10,241
( SCREAMING )

185
00:10:14,829 --> 00:10:15,830
( GRUNTING )

186
00:10:36,475 --> 00:10:37,893
( QUACKING )

187
00:10:37,977 --> 00:10:39,395
You seem so downcast.

188
00:10:39,645 --> 00:10:41,522
Has Mai gotten to you already?

189
00:10:41,605 --> 00:10:44,775
Though actually, Mai has been
in a strangely good mood lately.

190
00:10:45,359 --> 00:10:46,944
I haven't seen dad yet.

191
00:10:47,027 --> 00:10:50,364
I haven't seen him in three years,
since I was banished.

192
00:10:50,447 --> 00:10:51,699
AZULA: So what?

193
00:10:51,782 --> 00:10:54,034
So, I didn't capture the Avatar.

194
00:10:54,535 --> 00:10:56,912
Who cares? The Avatar's dead.

195
00:10:58,998 --> 00:11:03,252
Unless you think he somehow
miraculously survived.

196
00:11:05,379 --> 00:11:08,007
KATARA: This is water from
the spirit oasis at the North Pole.

197
00:11:08,299 --> 00:11:12,261
It has special properties, so I've been
saving it for something important.

198
00:11:13,637 --> 00:11:14,972
No.

199
00:11:15,055 --> 00:11:17,016
There's no way he could've survived.

200
00:11:21,854 --> 00:11:25,232
Well, then I'm sure you have
nothing to worry about.

201
00:11:40,247 --> 00:11:41,790
Load the Toph!

202
00:11:41,874 --> 00:11:43,375
( GRUNTING )

203
00:12:21,872 --> 00:12:23,249
I'm gonna give us some cover.

204
00:12:45,271 --> 00:12:47,856
I can't just stand by and do nothing.

205
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:49,066
Aang, no!

206
00:12:49,775 --> 00:12:52,528
You're still hurt,
and you have to stay secret.

207
00:12:52,611 --> 00:12:54,321
Just let us handle this.

208
00:12:55,030 --> 00:12:56,115
Fine.

209
00:13:07,459 --> 00:13:08,585
TOPH: How we doing?

210
00:13:08,669 --> 00:13:10,004
Things couldn't get much worse.

211
00:13:10,087 --> 00:13:12,298
( DRAGON GROWLING )

212
00:13:13,590 --> 00:13:16,844
The universe just loves
proving me wrong, doesn't it?

213
00:13:16,927 --> 00:13:18,304
You make it too easy.

214
00:13:31,859 --> 00:13:33,777
Thank you, the universe.

215
00:13:44,663 --> 00:13:45,956
Hey, Aang.

216
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,750
We're going into town to find some dinner.

217
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:49,460
( STOMACH GRUMBLING )

218
00:13:49,543 --> 00:13:51,587
Well, I am pretty hungry.

219
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:53,172
Maybe dinner's a good idea.

220
00:13:53,964 --> 00:13:55,382
Here, tie this around your head.

221
00:13:55,466 --> 00:13:56,800
It'll cover your arrow.

222
00:13:57,259 --> 00:14:00,095
I'm not going out
if I can't wear my arrow proudly.

223
00:14:00,637 --> 00:14:01,638
Aang, come on.

224
00:14:01,722 --> 00:14:02,723
Be practical.

225
00:14:03,474 --> 00:14:04,850
You guys go ahead without us.

226
00:14:04,933 --> 00:14:06,226
We'll catch up with you.

227
00:14:08,771 --> 00:14:12,441
I think I understand why
being a secret bothers you so much.

228
00:14:12,524 --> 00:14:14,401
You don't want people to think you failed.

229
00:14:14,485 --> 00:14:15,778
You're right, I don't.

230
00:14:15,861 --> 00:14:18,155
But the problem is, I did fail.

231
00:14:18,572 --> 00:14:20,407
Aang, that's not true.

232
00:14:20,491 --> 00:14:21,992
It is true.

233
00:14:22,076 --> 00:14:23,535
I was in Ba Sing Se.

234
00:14:23,619 --> 00:14:26,622
I was there, but I lost.

235
00:14:27,206 --> 00:14:29,291
And now, the Earth Kingdom
has fallen for good.

236
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,418
It's not for good.

237
00:14:31,502 --> 00:14:33,045
Remember, there's still a plan.

238
00:14:33,128 --> 00:14:34,296
The invasion.

239
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,423
And I hate the invasion plan, too.

240
00:14:36,507 --> 00:14:40,511
I don't want you or anyone else
risking your lives to fix my mistakes.

241
00:14:41,261 --> 00:14:44,056
I've always known
that I would have to face the Fire Lord

242
00:14:44,139 --> 00:14:45,849
But now I know I need to do it alone.

243
00:14:46,642 --> 00:14:47,976
Aang.

244
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,228
Katara, please.

245
00:14:49,770 --> 00:14:52,106
Just go, please.

246
00:14:54,191 --> 00:14:55,859
Is there anything you need?

247
00:14:57,653 --> 00:14:59,154
I need to redeem myself.

248
00:14:59,947 --> 00:15:01,907
I need my honor back.

249
00:15:12,751 --> 00:15:15,254
( SIGHING )

250
00:15:28,934 --> 00:15:30,269
I brought you some food.

251
00:15:33,188 --> 00:15:34,398
Oh, no.

252
00:15:50,414 --> 00:15:53,125
You have been away for a long time.

253
00:15:53,667 --> 00:15:56,462
I see the weight of your travels
has changed you.

254
00:15:57,004 --> 00:16:00,257
You have redeemed yourself, my son.

255
00:16:05,471 --> 00:16:07,181
Welcome home.

256
00:16:12,603 --> 00:16:13,979
[ ♪... ]

257
00:16:27,451 --> 00:16:29,411
I'll leave you two alone.

258
00:16:30,871 --> 00:16:32,206
What's wrong, Katara?

259
00:16:32,289 --> 00:16:33,457
He left.

260
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:34,541
What?

261
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:35,626
Aang.

262
00:16:35,709 --> 00:16:37,836
He just took his glider and disappeared.

263
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:41,965
He has this ridiculous notion
that he has to save the world alone

264
00:16:42,049 --> 00:16:43,717
That it's all his responsibility.

265
00:16:44,259 --> 00:16:46,428
Maybe that's his way of being brave.

266
00:16:46,512 --> 00:16:49,306
It's not brave. It's selfish and stupid.

267
00:16:49,389 --> 00:16:52,184
We could be helping him,
and I know the world needs him,

268
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:54,895
but doesn't he know how much
that we need him too?

269
00:16:54,978 --> 00:16:56,522
How could he just leave us behind?

270
00:16:58,398 --> 00:17:00,692
You're talking about me too, aren't you?

271
00:17:01,068 --> 00:17:03,487
How could you leave us, dad?

272
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:07,032
I mean, I know we had Gran-Gran,
and she loved us, but...

273
00:17:07,115 --> 00:17:09,701
But we were just so lost without you.

274
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,537
( SOBBING )

275
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:13,247
I'm so sorry, Katara.

276
00:17:16,041 --> 00:17:18,168
I understand why you left.

277
00:17:18,252 --> 00:17:22,214
I really do,
and I know that you had to go,

278
00:17:22,297 --> 00:17:25,884
so why do I still feel this way?

279
00:17:25,968 --> 00:17:29,972
I was so sad and angry, and hurt.

280
00:17:30,305 --> 00:17:33,100
I love you more than anything.

281
00:17:33,183 --> 00:17:35,686
You and your brother are my entire world.

282
00:17:36,103 --> 00:17:40,816
I thought about you every day I was gone,
and every night when I went to sleep

283
00:17:40,899 --> 00:17:44,987
I would lie awake
missing you so much it would ache.

284
00:17:48,532 --> 00:17:51,118
OZAI: I am proud of you, Prince Zuko.

285
00:17:51,201 --> 00:17:55,205
I am proud because you
and your sister conquered Ba Sing Se.

286
00:17:55,581 --> 00:18:00,877
I am proud because when your loyalty
was tested by your treacherous uncle

287
00:18:00,961 --> 00:18:04,506
you did the right thing
and captured the traitor

288
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:09,428
And I am proudest of all
of your most legendary accomplishment.

289
00:18:09,761 --> 00:18:12,347
You slayed the Avatar.

290
00:18:13,181 --> 00:18:14,349
What did you hear?

291
00:18:14,433 --> 00:18:16,059
Azula told me everything.

292
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:19,021
She said she was amazed and impressed

293
00:18:19,104 --> 00:18:24,151
with your power and ferocity
at the moment of truth.

294
00:18:31,283 --> 00:18:32,784
AANG: Blockade.

295
00:18:35,245 --> 00:18:36,413
( INHALING )

296
00:18:46,381 --> 00:18:47,883
( GASPING )

297
00:18:57,225 --> 00:18:58,477
( GRUNTING )

298
00:19:15,786 --> 00:19:16,870
( GRUNTING )

299
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:22,793
ZUKO: Why'd you do it?

300
00:19:24,336 --> 00:19:26,963
You're going to have to be
a little more specific.

301
00:19:27,506 --> 00:19:30,717
Why did you tell father
that I was the one who killed the Avatar?

302
00:19:30,801 --> 00:19:32,719
AZULA: Can't this wait until morning?

303
00:19:33,053 --> 00:19:34,304
It can't.

304
00:19:34,846 --> 00:19:36,473
( SIGHING ) Fine.

305
00:19:37,557 --> 00:19:40,060
You seemed so worried
about how father would treat you

306
00:19:40,143 --> 00:19:42,437
because you hadn't captured the Avatar.

307
00:19:42,521 --> 00:19:45,732
I figured, if I gave you the credit,
you'd have nothing to worry about.

308
00:19:45,816 --> 00:19:46,817
But why?

309
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:49,194
Call it a generous gesture.

310
00:19:49,277 --> 00:19:53,281
I wanted to thank you for your help,
and I was happy to share the glory.

311
00:19:53,532 --> 00:19:54,783
You're lying.

312
00:19:55,575 --> 00:19:56,827
If you say so.

313
00:19:57,494 --> 00:19:59,287
You have another motive for doing this.

314
00:19:59,371 --> 00:20:01,373
I just haven't figured out what it is.

315
00:20:01,456 --> 00:20:02,708
Please, Zuko.

316
00:20:03,083 --> 00:20:05,293
What ulterior motive could I have?

317
00:20:05,377 --> 00:20:07,087
What could I possibly gain

318
00:20:07,170 --> 00:20:10,507
by letting you get all the glory
for defeating the Avatar?

319
00:20:10,757 --> 00:20:14,511
Unless, somehow,
the Avatar was actually alive.

320
00:20:15,345 --> 00:20:19,599
All that glory would suddenly
turn to shame and foolishness.

321
00:20:21,184 --> 00:20:24,980
But you said yourself,
that was impossible.

322
00:20:25,897 --> 00:20:27,524
Sleep well, Zu Zu.

323
00:20:38,869 --> 00:20:41,621
( SCREAMING )

324
00:20:48,253 --> 00:20:50,297
( GASPING )

325
00:20:53,133 --> 00:20:55,343
I'm not gonna make it.

326
00:20:55,427 --> 00:20:56,428
I failed.

327
00:20:56,511 --> 00:20:58,680
( THUNDER RUMBLING )

328
00:20:58,764 --> 00:21:00,056
Roku?

329
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:02,225
You haven't failed, Aang.

330
00:21:02,934 --> 00:21:04,978
But everyone thinks I'm dead again.

331
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:09,775
They think I've abandoned them,
and I'm losing this war.

332
00:21:09,858 --> 00:21:11,818
I'm letting the whole world down.

333
00:21:12,152 --> 00:21:16,907
ROKU: If anyone is to blame
for the state of the world, it is me.

334
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:20,118
I should've seen this war coming,
and prevented it.

335
00:21:20,744 --> 00:21:25,207
You inherited my problems and my mistakes

336
00:21:25,290 --> 00:21:30,504
But I believe you are destined
to redeem me, and save the world.

337
00:21:30,879 --> 00:21:32,172
I don't know.

338
00:21:33,173 --> 00:21:35,300
YUE: You already saved the world.

339
00:21:38,428 --> 00:21:40,472
And you'll save the world again.

340
00:21:40,764 --> 00:21:42,891
But you can't give up.

341
00:21:47,687 --> 00:21:48,772
You're right.

342
00:21:49,189 --> 00:21:50,690
I won't give up.

343
00:22:29,312 --> 00:22:31,356
( CHIRPING )

344
00:22:34,025 --> 00:22:36,278
( GROANING )

345
00:22:40,448 --> 00:22:41,825
You're ok.

346
00:22:46,288 --> 00:22:48,665
( GROWLING )

347
00:22:51,251 --> 00:22:52,836
I have so much to do.

348
00:22:52,919 --> 00:22:54,963
I know, but you'll have our help.

349
00:22:55,046 --> 00:22:56,840
You didn't think
you could get out of training

350
00:22:56,923 --> 00:22:58,842
just by coming to the Fire Nation,
did you?

351
00:23:00,510 --> 00:23:02,053
What about the invasion?

352
00:23:02,137 --> 00:23:05,515
We'll join up with my dad and the invasion
force on the day of the eclipse.

353
00:23:05,599 --> 00:23:07,100
Hey, what's...

354
00:23:08,059 --> 00:23:10,812
Oh, it's your glider.

355
00:23:11,563 --> 00:23:12,856
That's ok.

356
00:23:14,691 --> 00:23:17,777
If someone saw it,
it would give away my identity.

357
00:23:18,236 --> 00:23:20,822
It's better for now
that no one knows I'm alive.

358
00:23:48,558 --> 00:23:50,018
[ ♪... ]
